   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b65c4f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### _Closeness_\n",
    "\n",
    "Probably relevant as well: \"Closeness centrality finds application in identifying individuals that are in a position to influence the entire network in the fastest way possible.\" (turing.com)\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Closeness was defined by Bavelas (1950) as the reciprocal of the farness\" (Wikipedia), so, normalised over the number of nodes, we get\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C(x_i) = (N-1)\\left(\\sum_{0 \\leq j < N}d(x_i, x_j)\\right)^{-1},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $d(x_i, x_j)$ is the shortest path between nodes $x_i$ and $x_j$. A fully-connected graph therefore has a closeness of 1 for each nodes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Due to the nature of its construction, this measure will not generate unique values for all nodes, which may be an issue when using this for ordering the nodes in a TEP.\n",
    "\n",
    "A variation on the closeness is the harmonic centrality, which has received less attention in academia. Mathematically, it is simply a matter of changing the order of the sum and inversion operators (and normalising accordingly):\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H(x_i) = \\frac{1}{N-1}\\sum_{0 \\leq j < N}\\left(\\frac{1}{d(x_i, x_j)}\\right).\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "0b65e1a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Text(0.5, 1.0, 'harmonic centrality distribution for $N=1000$\\nContains 75 unique values')"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 10,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 900x300 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# example: closeness and harmonic centrality\n",
    "N=1000; p=0.2\n",
    "G = ig.Graph.Erdos_Renyi(n=N, p=p)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axs = plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(9,3), sharey=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "closeness = G.closeness(normalized=True)\n",
    "closeness_unique = len(np.unique(np.array(closeness)))\n",
    "harmonic = G.harmonic_centrality(normalized=True)\n",
    "harmonic_unique = len(np.unique(np.array(harmonic)))\n",
    "\n",
    "bins=20 # None\n",
    "\n",
