   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In other words, we can choose the measure that we like most, as they are virtually identical."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8fdce659",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### _Betweenness_\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Measure for the number of shortest paths that pass through a node. Nodes with high betweenness centrality are critical for information flow. Their stability can enhance the overall robustness of the network.\" (ChatGPT)\n",
    "\n",
    "Mathematically, betweenness is calculated as follows:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "g(x_i) = \\sum_{j\\neq i}\\sum_{k\\neq i}\\frac{\\sigma_{jk}(x_i)}{\\sigma_{jk}},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $\\sigma_{jk}$ is the _total_ number of shortest paths from node $x_j$ to $x_k$, and $\\sigma_{jk}(x_i)$ is the number of those paths that pass through node $x_i$. Note that the sum only goes over nodes that are not identical to $x_i$, so the shortest paths can never end in $x_i$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Interestingly, betweenness is (typically) a unique value per node, so ordering would be straightforward."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f497f0df",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
