   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "73fd82ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### _Clustering coefficient_\n",
    "\n",
    "Also known as transitivity.\n",
    "\n",
    "\"A measure of the degree to which nodes in a graph tend to cluster together.\n",
    "High clustering can enhance local robustness, as tightly-knit clusters may stabilize each other.\" (ChatGPT)\n",
    "\n",
    "This measure is particularly relevant for Watts-Strogatz graphs (and they came up with it). The centrality of node $x_i$ is defined as (Wikipedia)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C_i = \\frac{2|\\{e_{jk} : x_j, x_k \\in \\mathcal{N}(x_i), e_{jk} \\in E\\}|}{|\\mathcal{N}(x_i)||\\mathcal{N}(x_i)-1|},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $\\mathcal{N}(x_i)$ is the neighbourhood of node $x_i$ excluding node $x_i$ itself (more simply put: $|\\mathcal{x_i}|$ is simply the degree of node $x_i$). This is identical to saying that\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C_i = \\frac{\\lambda_G(x_i)}{\\tau_G(x_i)},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $\\lambda_G(x_i)$ is the number of triangles on $x_i$, and $\\tau_G(x_i)$ is the number of triples on $x_i$. Note that, because $\\tau_G(x_i) \\geq \\lambda_G(x_i)$, $C_i$ is always between 0 and 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "547a9edc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<matplotlib.legend.Legend at 0x265cc893cd0>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 28,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
